    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23287" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-frăgĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>that cannot be broken to pieces.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adamas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. H. N. 20</span></i>
			 prooem. § 2.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>strong</i>, <i>that cannot be weakened</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 1, 5, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Vit. B. 9</span></i>
			.</div>
